---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Course Explorer">
  <h1>Course Explorer</h1>
  <p>
    A mock replacement for the part of ANU's enrolment system that makes you
    look a course up on one site, copy its class number, then paste it into a
    completely different one that shows you no course content at all. Here
    the course descriptions and the timetable live in the same place.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Everything in the catalog is fictional</strong> — course codes,
    titles and descriptions are invented for this prototype, not copied from
    any real ANU offering.
  </p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a class="button" href="/courses/">Browse the course catalog</a>
    <a class="button button-secondary" href="/timetable/">Go to my timetable</a>
  </div>
  <p>
    Enrol in a course from the catalog, then head to <a href="/timetable/">my timetable</a>
    to pick a tutorial time for it — hovering an option previews where it'd
    sit on the week before you commit to it, and clashes with what you've
    already picked are highlighted, not blocked.
  </p>
</Base>
